Fixed degree appears to simplify LV6 substantially. It may allow character primes with polynomially many bits and at most one exceptional square class, uniformly over the fields here. If that argument checks out, it avoids a separate probability bound under the kept-field law. I’m also writing out a Hensel square-root algorithm so its cost does not rest on an implementation citation.
