The HECM caveat has two possible resolutions. The genus-2 separation proof and LPP I’s unconditional smooth-number bound appear to give the required test for every smooth input. Separately, batching all candidates in a capped special-\(q\) search costs \((B+S^2)L^{o(1)}\); at Theorem A’s optimum, \(S^2\) exceeds \(B\). That would remove HECM without paying A′’s exponent penalty.
