+On \(H_S\), use the unramified quadratic Frobenius character, normalizing any even valuation by a local square. It is consequently well defined on square classes. On the atomic products here, which are units at these primes, it is exactly the displayed residue symbol.
+
+With \(J=C\log N\), a union bound gives
+
+\[
+\Pr(\ker\chi\text{ contains a nonexceptional nonzero class})
+\le |H_S|(1-1/(4d))^J\le N^{-2}.
+\]
+
