+
+The matrix has at most the stated column count and \(O(m\log N)\) nonzero entries. Use [Kaltofen–Saunders (1991), Theorems 2–4 and §2](https://kaltofen.math.ncsu.edu/bibliography/91/KaSa91.pdf), the rigorous singular-system Wiedemann method, over \(\mathbb F_{2^w}\) of cardinality at least \(m^4\). Zero-padding handles rectangular matrices; Toeplitz preconditioning preserves fast multiplication. Their rank error is \(O(m^2/2^w)\), and the cost is \(O(m)\) matrix applications plus \(\widetilde O(m^2)\) field operations. Expand extension-field solutions in an \(\mathbb F_2\)-basis, retaining two independent binary kernel vectors; verify them and retry on failure. Their uniform-solution theorem gives constant expected retries. Bit cost is \(m^{2+o(1)}\).
+
+For two independent dependencies \(s_1,s_2\), at least one of \(s_1,s_2,s_1+s_2\) has trivial algebraic square class. Test these three directly. This avoids searching a class group or guessing that quadratic characters have eliminated every obstruction.
